message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "HASH$CyberAxe: replay kits"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jeremy
    family-names: Benisek
    alias: CyberAxe
    website: "https://cyberaxe.dev/"
url: "https://hashcyberaxe.com/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jbenisek/hash-cyberaxe-replay-kits"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-11-06"
abstract: "Small, self-contained kits that each reproduce one published HASH$CyberAxe result, recount or teaching example from its saved data. Every kit has its own README, the exact input files and check_project.py, which verifies the files and, with --replay, reruns the kit's finite replay. Use them to check a claim yourself, learn a method on a small worked example, or start a fork."
keywords:
  - cryptanalysis
  - SHA-256
  - BLAKE3
  - SHA-3
  - Poseidon
  - reproducibility
